  "solution": {
    "text": "Photochemical smog, also known as &#39;Oxidising smog&#39; is an atmospheric condition that produces various unwanted effects such as eye irritation and poor visibility.<br /><br />The main ingredients of photochemical smog include energy from sunlight, hydrocarbons and oxides of nitrogen.<br /><br />The name &#39;Oxidising smog&#39; is given because it contains high concentration of oxidising agents.",
